    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d714">

                <pb facs="0936" n="837" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg837"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/8458½: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chilean Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cruchaga</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Assistant
                        Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-06-04">June 4, 1936</date>.<lb/>[Received June 4—8:20
                        p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Truly regret scope and purpose attached to our memorandum. At no time have we
                    doubted lofty intentions your Government and the very wording of memorandum
                    shows our complete confidence in attitude United States. My desire has been to
                    cooperate with you in warding off such disturbing requests by warning the
                    governments which may wish to formulate or share in one of them that we are
                    unalterably opposed thereto.</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Miguel Cruchaga</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
